            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Either dilate horizontally by a factor of ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "\\frac12",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " and then translate right 3 units, or translate right 6 units and then dilate horizontally by a factor of ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "\\frac12",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ". Factorising reveals the first sequence but is not required.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "Mary is correct. Dilating horizontally by a factor of $\\frac12$ replaces $x$ by $2x$. Translating the resulting graph right 3 units replaces $x$ by $x-3$:\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=f(2x)\\\\y&=f\\bigl(2(x-3)\\bigr)=f(2x-6).\\end{align*}$$\nAlternatively, translate right 6 units first, then dilate horizontally by a factor of $\\frac12$:\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=f(x-6)\\\\y&=f(2x-6).\\end{align*}$$\nBoth sequences give the required graph, so factorising is helpful but not necessary.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
